                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dd278b13-5958-3e6f-8c7a-3418f9ff44f7",
                        "entry_id": "9a67a592-03b8-3cf9-a50b-35ab04df9f5c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "joods leraar met de hoogste bevoegdheid, ook bevoegd om te antwoorden en beslissen bij halachische kwesties, vaak verbonden aan een joodse gemeente en daarbij belast met onderwijs en zielzorg, tevens een religieuze, joodse geleerde die een expert is op het gebied van joodse wetgeving"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "beroep",
                            "Jiddisch-Hebreeuws"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c142a296-4911-45bd-919e-b12e394b95a7",
                        "source_entry_id": "9a67a592-03b8-3cf9-a50b-35ab04df9f5c",
                        "source_sense_id": "dd278b13-5958-3e6f-8c7a-3418f9ff44f7",
                        "target_lang_word": "Rabbiner",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Rabbiner",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "22b1b3a8-724a-3b7d-8339-115091e22e9b",
                                        "entry_id": "0a0c91c1-753e-330e-9f88-cd0110fb5f1b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "jüdischer Gesetzes- und Religionslehrer, Prediger und Seelsorger"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Judentum"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33544925-52fd-4e0c-8c1e-892d66edbe29",
                                                "sense_id": "22b1b3a8-724a-3b7d-8339-115091e22e9b",
                                                "text": "„Vier Jahre vor dem Jahr 2000 darf in Israel noch immer kein Jude eine Muslimin heiraten, die Luftfahrtgesellschaft El Al stellt samstags ihre Flüge ein, Zucht und Einfuhr von Schweinen ist gesetzlich verboten, die Rabbiner verhindern Autopsien, und jedesmal wenn eine Baugrube ausgehoben wird, kommt es zu Demonstrationen von Ultrareligiösen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8456e107-9e6d-4883-b34c-ffbae100d6e8",
                                                "sense_id": "22b1b3a8-724a-3b7d-8339-115091e22e9b",
                                                "text": "„Auf den sich mit Inkrafttreten dieser Verordnung im Amt befindlichen Rabbiner finden die Bestimmungen der Verordnung vom 8. Mai 1996 über die Pfarrwahlen […] betreffend die Neuwahl keine Anwendung.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f9fb9e1-f48c-4814-b73e-29eeca5d621f",
                                                "sense_id": "22b1b3a8-724a-3b7d-8339-115091e22e9b",
                                                "text": "„Prosper Chetrit, auch er schon 78 Jahre alt und seit dem Tod seiner Mutter der letzte Jude in Oran, weist darauf hin, dass 3 000 Juden über 1962 hinaus in Oran geblieben waren: \"Für sie wurde es erst nach 1971 schlimm, als ihre Synagoge in eine Moschee umgewandelt wurde und der letzte Rabbiner wegging. Aber ich kann nicht klagen, alle wissen, dass ich Jude bin, und alle schätzen mich.\"“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bee9f34e-1f6e-4ee2-82ef-b07d22a0bb17",
                                                "sense_id": "22b1b3a8-724a-3b7d-8339-115091e22e9b",
                                                "text": "„Nachdem der Rabbiner also gesprochen hatte, verschwand er.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e6425797-9345-456b-94ee-c246b06e643f",
                        "source_entry_id": "9a67a592-03b8-3cf9-a50b-35ab04df9f5c",
                        "source_sense_id": "dd278b13-5958-3e6f-8c7a-3418f9ff44f7",
                        "target_lang_word": "rabbi",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rabbi",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b94ac8ee-aa1a-3304-b8e9-4e9d057dcb4f",
                                        "entry_id": "980fc190-4492-37e1-82ea-5d5c8e99215b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A Jewish scholar or teacher of halacha (Jewish law), capable of making halachic decisions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f2b6f43a-7752-4e0e-b85f-978b66629889",
                                                "sense_id": "b94ac8ee-aa1a-3304-b8e9-4e9d057dcb4f",
                                                "text": "Next, R. Moskowitz brings us to the Slonimer Rebbe, a late 20th century Hasidic rabbi, who taught that the evil of Esav was that very sense of completion, the self-perception that he had no need for growth or further transformation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "08b0bb1e-6f3f-359b-ba2e-2f41747136bc",
                                        "entry_id": "980fc190-4492-37e1-82ea-5d5c8e99215b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A Jew who is the leader or is qualified to be the leader of a Jewish congregation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c20d919-cdf7-4c5d-a623-e25dec5b6749",
                                                "sense_id": "08b0bb1e-6f3f-359b-ba2e-2f41747136bc",
                                                "text": "\"Elon Musk is spreading the kind of antisemitism that leads to massacres,\" reads the decree, which was signed by 164 \"rabbis, leaders of Jewish organizations, artists, activists, and academics.\" \"And advertisers are funding the platform that allows him to spread his ideology to hundreds of millions [of] people.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "80701f98-f7cf-3520-bb86-300222ced788",
                                        "entry_id": "980fc190-4492-37e1-82ea-5d5c8e99215b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A senior officer who acts as a mentor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7df3eb61-2833-46e0-ab29-93d54e72d53e",
                                                "sense_id": "80701f98-f7cf-3520-bb86-300222ced788",
                                                "text": "Hoskins? He doesn't have a better rabbi in the department than that?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24c1f242-b04e-4892-bd75-cc2ece96ea2a",
                                                "sense_id": "80701f98-f7cf-3520-bb86-300222ced788",
                                                "text": "If I'm ever gonna make Captain, I need a good mentor. I need my rabbi."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "be48dba1-18c0-4632-9351-699f1644c297",
                        "source_entry_id": "9a67a592-03b8-3cf9-a50b-35ab04df9f5c",
                        "source_sense_id": "dd278b13-5958-3e6f-8c7a-3418f9ff44f7",
                        "target_lang_word": "rebbe",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rebbe",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a5800cd2-5a6a-3a13-914e-b6c055cc2003",
                                        "entry_id": "24ee213d-223e-3c48-9eb0-145a07776229",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The spiritual leader of a Hasidic Jewish community."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Judaism"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f98117c9-53f1-40c1-b70b-0de3b2b566cc",
                                                "sense_id": "a5800cd2-5a6a-3a13-914e-b6c055cc2003",
                                                "text": "Born in Riga in 1909 into a vast cousinage that included the Lubavitcher rebbes, Isaiah Mendelevich Berlin was taken to Petrograd as a small boy, and then to London in 1921 when the Bolsheviks allowed his prosperous (and fortunate) parents to leave."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "741e3f11-15bd-4bda-92eb-67398250bd68",
                                                "sense_id": "a5800cd2-5a6a-3a13-914e-b6c055cc2003",
                                                "text": "But two men who said they spoke with some of those who broke through the synagogue wall said the motive was to hasten an expansion of 770 — a move that they say the Lubavitcher movement’s leader, Rabbi Menachem Mendel Schneerson, known as the rebbe, called for more than three decades ago."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4df6e6de-173b-4bae-a84d-83633484b276",
                        "source_entry_id": "9a67a592-03b8-3cf9-a50b-35ab04df9f5c",
                        "source_sense_id": "dd278b13-5958-3e6f-8c7a-3418f9ff44f7",
                        "target_lang_word": "rabbin",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rabbin",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "92373bba-1ed5-3d13-910f-a72a066933d0",
                                        "entry_id": "2ade84bf-5bca-3c63-9131-7605be452090",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Docteur des juifs ; ministre du culte judaïque."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Judaism"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e3c4a27-b874-4c4f-806f-9f5861401632",
                                                "sense_id": "92373bba-1ed5-3d13-910f-a72a066933d0",
                                                "text": "Or, c’était fête à la synagogue, ténébreusement étoilée de lampes d’argent, et les rabbins, en robes et en lunettes, baisaient leurs talmuds, marmottant, nasillonnant, crachant ou se mouchant, les uns assis, les autres non."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba91bafc-cbaa-487a-9077-a45c9b2d724d",
                                                "sense_id": "92373bba-1ed5-3d13-910f-a72a066933d0",
                                                "text": "[…] alors que jusqu’au huitième siècle, nous n’avons connaissance d’aucun rabbin célèbre en France, on voit apparaître à cette époque, et précisément à Narbonne, un talmudiste de valeur, nommé Makhir et originaire de Babylonie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b3bf9c2-de70-40d0-bc2e-c0bf45786c75",
                                                "sense_id": "92373bba-1ed5-3d13-910f-a72a066933d0",
                                                "text": "Au point de vue juridique, les juifs relevaient de leurs rabbins et de la loi mosaïque dans les question de statut personnel ; pour le reste ils étaient justiciables, comme les musulmans, des caïds et des cadis."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd509085-2c38-42c6-bc31-7808365c5dee",
                                                "sense_id": "92373bba-1ed5-3d13-910f-a72a066933d0",
                                                "text": "Une dizaine de mioches assis sur une natte en raphia ânonnaient en chœur l’alphabet hébraïque dessiné sur une planche en bois d’arar (thuya) sur laquelle le rabbin promenait son doigt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f62ec5c5-befc-4eff-95c4-13bfdf8ec77b",
                                                "sense_id": "92373bba-1ed5-3d13-910f-a72a066933d0",
                                                "text": "Les rabbins sont exactement aussi pervers et avides de pouvoir que leurs collègues des églises et mollahcraties ou autres exploiteurs de la fragilité mentale-affective humaine de par le monde."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ad9eb4f-bb7c-48fa-a07a-cf5380094783",
                                                "sense_id": "92373bba-1ed5-3d13-910f-a72a066933d0",
                                                "text": "« Unir nos forces contre le fondamentalisme, qui est un dévoiement du religieux », soutient, madame Pauline Bebe, rabbin, membre du collège des fondateurs…"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c93c00b5-36e8-466d-a3b3-10a786f084e9",
